# Phase 1: Business discovery

**Owner:** Product manager. **Participants:** Sponsor, operations lead, sales/customer support representative. **Timebox:** First 30 minutes of discovery.

## Objective and known context

Define how the business makes money and fulfills a customer promise before discussing features. The confirmed brief is a custom production e-commerce platform using the stack recorded in [the planning index](../README.md). Company identity, product category, sales volume, customer demographics, and current systems have not been supplied.

Working model: a single merchant selling physical goods in Bangladesh, in BDT, with one stock location. Validate D01-D03; do not present this as an existing business profile.

## Meeting sequence

| Minutes | Topic | Questions and evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 0-5 | Company and commercial model | What is sold, to whom, through which channels? Ask for catalog examples and the operating entity |
| 5-12 | Customer journey | How do buyers find, compare, order, pay, and get support? Walk through one real order |
| 12-20 | Fulfillment and finance | Who checks stock, packs, ships, handles returns, and reconciles money? Review redacted records |
| 20-25 | Goals and constraints | Which outcomes matter in the next six months? What cannot change at launch? |
| 25-30 | Validate understanding | Read back workflow, risks, owners, and the next evidence requests |

## Workflow to document

Discovery -> product selection -> stock and price confirmation -> checkout -> verified payment -> fulfillment approval -> pick and pack -> courier handoff -> delivery -> support or return -> refund and settlement reconciliation.

For each step record the actor, system or spreadsheet, input, output, typical delay, exception, and escalation owner. Capture failed payments, out-of-stock orders, delivery failures, and damaged returns separately.

## Business record

| Field | Current planning position | Confirmation owner |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Business name and contracting entity | Not provided | Sponsor |
| Product categories and restrictions | Not provided; physical goods assumed | Product owner |
| Sales channels | Website proposed; physical stores/social channels unknown | Sales |
| Customers and service areas | Bangladesh assumed; segments and delivery coverage unknown | Sales + operations |
| Revenue and margin model | Retail sales assumed; actual margins and costs unknown | Finance |
| Existing operations | No evidence supplied | Operations |
| Success definition | Fewer order errors, reliable payments/stock, faster fulfillment proposed | Sponsor |
| Constraints | Technology stack supplied; budget and launch date unknown | Sponsor |

## Outputs and completion

Produce a one-page business summary, current workflow, stakeholder list, evidence requests, and updated D01-D03/D12 assumptions. Request aggregated or redacted operational evidence; avoid copying customer personal data into planning documents.

Complete when operations confirms the workflow and the sponsor names the business outcome owner. Do not promise an exact price, delivery date, or feature list in this meeting.
